Z||000000||Avery Montembeault||08-31-2001||11:25 AM||||been considering swapping out my iron duke for a v6 cause I cant afford the v8 swap kit. Ive been told a 3.4 is a good v6 and the stock fiero air intake will bolt on. Do I need to adapt anything or will the engine bolt right into my izuzu 5 speed? what about brakets, altenator etc.? figured id go yank an engine out of an old camero or something..||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||08-31-2001||11:56 AM||||You'll want to search the forum and/or the archives for more in depth info.  <P>But the 4cyl to V6 swap should be pretty easy.  The 3.4 is currently the best choice of block. The 2.8, 3.1, and 3.4 are physically all the same.  Same mounts & same tranny hookup, but some minor mods are required (relocating the starter from RWD-type to FWD-type). Hopefully you can get wiring from another Fiero V6 (junkyard) that will make the install easier too.  The only thing that could be a hinder is if the car is an '84.  There was another post earlier today stating that the '84 didn't have the V6 wiring pre-installed, whereas the 85 and later models all had the V6 wiring even if it just had a 4cyl.  Hope this helps to at least get you on the right track!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
